    description: `Zeitgeist — the spirit of the time — was popularized by German Romantic philosophers, particularly Hegel, who argued that history progresses through the unfolding of a collective spirit. Today it describes the dominant cultural attitudes, assumptions, and anxieties of an era. To 'capture the zeitgeist' is to make something that feels precisely of its moment.`,
