    partOfSpeech: `noun`,
    meaning: `A manuscript where earlier writing has been erased but traces remain; anything showing layered history.`,
    description: `Medieval scribes would scrape clean expensive parchment and reuse it, but the original text would often show through — a ghost of earlier meaning beneath the new. Scholars have recovered lost ancient texts using this palimpsest effect. As a metaphor, it describes any object, place, or person whose history shows through their present form: cities are palimpsests; so are people.`,
