    partOfSpeech: `adjective`,
    meaning: `Of a definition: given by direct demonstration rather than verbal description.`,
    description: `An ostensive definition shows rather than tells. To define 'red' ostensively, you point to red things. Ludwig Wittgenstein examined the limits of ostensive definition: pointing at something doesn't guarantee shared understanding — the learner must already know that you're indicating color, not shape or texture. Ostensive teaching is fundamental in early language acquisition.`,
