    description: `Leon Festinger proposed cognitive dissonance theory in 1957 after studying a cult that predicted the end of the world. When the world didn't end, members didn't abandon their belief — they doubled down. The theory explains why people rationalize bad decisions, why smokers find reasons smoking isn't that harmful, and why we are all, to some degree, defenders of our past choices.`,
