    type: "word",
    phonetic: `/ˈpræk.sɪs/`,
    partOfSpeech: `noun`,
    meaning: `The process of enacting a theory or idea into practice.`,
    description: `Praxis is the bridge between theory and action — it is not merely applying ideas but the cycle through which action tests and refines theory. Central to Marxist and critical pedagogy thought, particularly Paulo Freire's Pedagogy of the Oppressed, where praxis means reflection and action upon the world in order to transform it.`,
