    type: "word",
    phonetic: `/ˈɒs.trə.saɪz/`,
    partOfSpeech: `verb`,
    meaning: `To exclude someone from a group or society.`,
    description: `From the Athenian practice of ostraka — citizens would scratch the name of someone deemed dangerous to democracy onto a pottery shard. If 6,000 votes were cast, the named person was exiled for ten years. The system was designed to prevent tyranny. The word now means any form of social exclusion.`,
