    description: `Originally a Greek religious term for something set apart — dedicated to divine destruction. The early Christian church used anathema to denote the most severe form of excommunication. Today it means anything intensely opposed or abhorrent, often in ideological or intellectual contexts: 'That argument is anathema to everything I believe.'`,
