    type: "word",
    phonetic: `/ˌek.wəˈnɪm.ɪ.ti/`,
    partOfSpeech: `noun`,
    meaning: `Mental calmness and composure, especially in difficult situations.`,
    description: `Equanimity is the Stoic ideal in everyday English — the capacity to remain undisturbed by circumstance. Unlike apathy (not caring) or forced cheerfulness, equanimity acknowledges difficulty while maintaining steadiness. Buddhist practice also cultivates equanimity (upekkhā) as one of the four divine abodes. It requires neither suppression of feeling nor surrender to it.`,
