    type: "word",
    phonetic: `/ˈhjuː.brɪs/`,
    partOfSpeech: `noun`,
    meaning: `Excessive pride or self-confidence, especially when leading to downfall.`,
    description: `In Greek tragedy, hubris was the fatal flaw: the moment a hero's pride exceeded proper bounds and offended the gods. Nemesis — divine retribution — invariably followed. The concept remains central to leadership analysis, business post-mortems, and political history: nearly every great fall involves a period of hubris. The structure is so reliable it functions as a predictive pattern.`,
