    type: "word",
    phonetic: `/ˈtæs.ɪt/`,
    partOfSpeech: `adjective`,
    meaning: `Understood or implied without being stated; silent.`,
    description: `Michael Polanyi's concept of tacit knowledge revolutionized epistemology: 'We know more than we can tell.' Much of what experts know cannot be fully articulated — it lives in skilled performance, intuition, and the body. Tacit knowledge is why reading a manual never fully replaces apprenticeship. In contracts and agreements, tacit consent or understanding operates similarly.`,
