    description: `The etymology is disputed but delightfully strange — possibly from Greek for 'fig revealer,' referring to informers who revealed illegal fig exports. Today it describes the classic yes-man: someone whose agreement is determined by self-interest rather than truth. Identifying sycophants around leaders is essential — surrounded by them, leaders lose touch with reality.`,
