    phonetic: `/ˈɑː.bɪ.trɑːʒ/`,
    partOfSpeech: `noun`,
    meaning: `The practice of exploiting a price difference between two markets for profit.`,
    description: `Classical arbitrage is risk-free profit from price differences — buy cheap in one market, sell expensive in another simultaneously. In modern usage it extends to any exploitation of asymmetric information or opportunity: career arbitrage (skills undervalued in one field that are prized in another), geographic arbitrage (earning in strong currency while living where costs are low), status arbitrage.`,
