    type: "word",
    phonetic: `/ˌɒk.əlˈteɪ.ʃ(ə)n/`,
    partOfSpeech: `noun`,
    meaning: `The concealment of one celestial body by another; more broadly, the hiding of something.`,
    description: `In astronomy, an occultation occurs when one body passes in front of another and hides it — the moon occulting a star, a planet occulting a moon. As a metaphor, it describes anything that obscures or hides: the occultation of important facts in a report, or the way institutional language occultes what is actually happening.`,
