    type: "word",
    phonetic: `/prəˈpɪŋ.kwɪ.ti/`,
    partOfSpeech: `noun`,
    meaning: `Nearness in place, time, or relationship; proximity.`,
    description: `The propinquity effect is well-documented in social psychology: we tend to like and trust people we are physically near. Roommates become friends; office neighbors collaborate more; neighbors marry. In an age of remote work, propinquity effects weaken and must be consciously replaced. The word itself is underused and pleasantly precise.`,
