    phonetic: `/ˌes.əˈter.ɪk/`,
    partOfSpeech: `adjective`,
    meaning: `Intended for or understood by a small group with specialized knowledge.`,
    description: `Esoteric knowledge was originally that reserved for initiates — the inner circle of a philosophical school or mystery cult. Today it describes anything requiring deep specialist knowledge: esoteric financial instruments, esoteric academic debates, esoteric music subgenres. The opposite, exoteric, describes what is publicly accessible. The tension between esoteric and exoteric knowledge structures many institutions.`,
