    partOfSpeech: `adjective`,
    meaning: `Tending to obstruct or harm; unfriendly; hostile.`,
    description: `Inimical describes something fundamentally opposed or harmful — not accidentally but by its nature. Climate is inimical to certain crops; bureaucracy can be inimical to innovation; certain ideologies are inimical to free expression. It implies deeper incompatibility than mere conflict — the hostility is structural.`,
