    partOfSpeech: `German expression`,
    meaning: `A configuration or pattern of elements so unified that it cannot be understood by analyzing its parts separately.`,
    description: `The Gestalt principle — 'the whole is different from the sum of its parts' — was a revolutionary insight in psychology. The mind organizes perceptions into unified wholes: you perceive a face, not individual features. This has permeated design (Gestalt principles of visual organization), therapy (Gestalt therapy), and everyday usage for any situation where the overall pattern is what matters.`,
