    partOfSpeech: `noun`,
    meaning: `The insertion of something between existing elements; the addition of a day or month into a calendar.`,
    description: `Intercalation in calendars — adding leap days or leap months — corrects the drift between human timekeeping and astronomical reality. In chemistry, intercalation describes molecules inserting between layers. In everyday use it's a precise word for inserting new elements without disrupting existing structure: intercalating a new step into an established process.`,
