    meaning: `The tendency toward disorder; a measure of the unavailability of energy for useful work.`,
    description: `The second law of thermodynamics: in a closed system, entropy always increases. Disorder is the natural direction of things; order requires energy to maintain. As a metaphor, entropy describes the natural tendency of organizations, relationships, and projects to degrade without maintenance. Understanding entropy is understanding why things fall apart and why maintenance is not optional.`,
