    description: `Heterodox thinkers work against the grain of their discipline's consensus. Sometimes they are wrong and appropriately marginalized; sometimes they are right and eventually vindicated. The history of science and economics is full of heterodox ideas that became orthodoxy: continental drift, H. pylori causing ulcers, index funds. Identifying which heterodox ideas deserve attention is a high-skill task.`,
