    meaning: `Excessively long or technical speech or writing; an abundance of words.`,
    description: `Verbiage is the enemy of clarity. It inflates, obscures, and exhausts readers. Legal documents, bureaucratic memos, and academic papers are prone to verbiage — saying in 200 words what could be said in 20. Stripping verbiage is one of the core disciplines of good writing. The diagnosis is simple: if removing a word changes nothing, remove it.`,
