    meaning: `Relieving symptoms without treating the underlying cause; a measure that provides temporary relief.`,
    description: `Palliative care relieves suffering without curing disease. In everyday use, a palliative measure addresses symptoms rather than causes — useful when the cause cannot be fixed, but dangerous when it substitutes for treating the real problem. Recognizing whether an intervention is palliative or curative clarifies strategic thinking in medicine, policy, and organizations.`,
